From 970514e28c49ed48e5bb947f80f05bd3929ae472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Wedgwood <cw@f00f.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:07:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(usb_serial_jtag): stop false disconnects from SOF
 read/clear race

The connection monitor tick hook reads SOF_INT_RAW and then clears it in
a separate write. A SOF that arrives between the read and the clear is
cleared without being seen. The FreeRTOS tick (chip crystal) and the
host's 1 ms frames are independent clocks, so their phase drifts through
that window periodically and the hook sees false "no SOF" samples while
the host is attached and sending frames. The hardware frame number shows
it: on every such sample the received frame number had advanced.

The allowance of ALLOWED_NO_SOF_TICKS is also only refilled on
reconnect, so isolated misses accumulate over the whole uptime. Together
these report a disconnect while the host is attached and streaming,
after which reads and writes fail with EIO (fatal for an OpenThread RCP
using the USB-Serial/JTAG port as its Spinel link:
esp_openthread_uart_process() returns ESP_FAIL and the main loop hits
assert(false)).

Fix:
- add usb_serial_jtag_ll_get_frame_num() and treat a change in the
  received frame number as a SOF; it advances with every SOF and cannot
  be lost between read and clear;
- refill the allowance on every SOF while connected, so only consecutive
  SOF-less ticks count.

Measured with per-minute counters (ticks, SOF-less ticks, disconnects,
frames) on OpenThread RCPs using USB-Serial/JTAG. Offset = (frames -
ticks) / ticks between chip and host.

Without the fix (current code):
- ESP32-C5 v1.0, Windows PC, -3.0 ppm: 176 false disconnects in 6.5 h
- ESP32-H2 v0.2, same PC, ~0.9 ppm: 80 in 3.0 h

With the fix (target: 0), 0 false disconnects and 0 EIO on every board:
- ESP32-C5 v1.0: Windows PC (-3.0 ppm), 4.4 h; Intel Alder Lake xHCI
  (+25.9 ppm), 19.9 h
- ESP32-H2 v0.2: Raspberry Pi 4 VL805 (-129 ppm, a window crossing every
  7.5 s), 10.8 h; Intel ICH10 UHCI (-2.7 ppm), 11.2 h
- ESP32-C6 v0.1: Raspberry Pi 4 VL805 (-140 ppm), 6.3 h, ~3,200
  crossings
- ESP32-C6 v0.0: Intel ICH10 UHCI (~0 ppm, drifting through zero),
  6.9 h; each crossing lasted a whole minute (770 and 1,522 flag
  misses)
In total about 10,000 window crossings and about 2,000 isolated true
misses without a false disconnect. The refill keeps the isolated misses
(about one a minute at -129 ppm) from accumulating into a disconnect;
with the frame-number check alone the C5 still had 2 false disconnects
in 4.2 h.

Compiled and linked for esp32c3/c5/c6/c61/h2/h21/h4/p4/s3/s31.

Related: #18490, #13935
